DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027
 : Energy Ghosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Mensch Maschine VISIT R
 esidency Program is an annual fellowship offering four fully funded fellow
 ships to artists from around the world\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the 
 Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with VISIT\, the artist-in-residence program
 me of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centr
 e for Contemporary Art (Warsaw).\n\nOrganisation: JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Ak
 ademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujaz
 dowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocation: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, 
 Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie der Künste\, Berlin (1 fel
 low)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to
  artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fellowships of EUR 20\,000 e
 ach\, intended for artist fees and production costs of a new project (rese
 arch and development\, travel\, materials and presentation costs)\, plus s
 tudio space and accommodation for the three-month residency.\nDuration: Ab
 out three months\, mid-August to mid-November 2027: retreat at Ujazdowski 
 Castle in Warsaw in mid-August\, then the residency at E-WERK Luckenwalde 
 or Akademie der Künste Berlin from late August\, ending with a symposium 
 at the Akademie der Künste on 5 and 6 November 2027. Fellows must be avai
 lable from 13 August to 10 November 2027 and live and work on site at leas
 t 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-m
 aschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hiig-impact-ai-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T134737Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Deadline: HIIG Impact AI Fellowship 2027 (EUR 5\,000\, 10 weeks\, B
 erlin and remote)
DESCRIPTION:HIIG's Impact AI Fellowship invites people interested in measur
 ing the effects of AI on society and the environment to assess an existing
 \, operational AI application and take lead authorship of a published case
  report. Applicants do not need their own case\; HIIG helps match fellows 
 with cases\, and proposed cases must be deployed applications rather than 
 prototypes or research ideas.\n\nOrganisation: Alexander von Humboldt Inst
 itute for Internet and Society (HIIG)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany (two man
 datory in-person weeks\; other weeks can be remote). No nationality restri
 ction stated.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 fixed stipend per fellow for the ten week
 s (inclusive of any tax or social security in the fellow's home country)\,
  with case-by-case partial support for in-person costs. No application fee
  mentioned.\nDuration: 10 weeks\, 16 August to 22 October 2027\, with in-p
 erson weeks in Berlin on 16-20 August and 4-8 October 2027 and a mandatory
  online preparatory session on 11 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiig.de/e
 n/impact-ai-call-for-fellows/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.hiig.de/en/impact-ai-call-for-fellows/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (two mandatory in-person weeks\; other weeks can 
 be remote). No nationality restriction stated.
END:VEVENT
